.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt WRITE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm write
.Nd write to a scheme-file handle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
See the
.Pa raven-abi
crate (syscall number 0x63).
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The .Nm system call is part of the scheme IPC protocol (see
.Xr scheme 7
and
.Pa architecture/03-system-servers.md ).
.Pp
Filesystem
.Nm
is sequential.  The server writes at the cursor in the open-file description and
advances it by the number of bytes written.  The wire offset must be zero; a
server returns
.Er EINVAL
for a nonzero offset.
.Pp
With
.Dv WIRE_OPEN_APPEND
(see
.Xr open 2 )
each write is placed at the file's length at the time of that write, atomically
at the server even when other descriptions write concurrently.  The writing
description's cursor is left at the end of the write.
.Pp
A
.Xr dup 2
or a transferred reference shares the description and its cursor.  The server
releases unlinked data only at the last
.Xr close 2 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The number of bytes written.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er -offset indent
.It Er EINVAL
The wire offset was nonzero.
.It Er EBADF
The handle is not open for writing.
.It Er EISDIR
The handle names a directory.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr close 2 ,
.Xr dup 2 ,
.Xr open 2 ,
.Xr read 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
